# Copy to ".private-terms" (gitignored) and list anything that should never be
# published from this repo — one term per line, case-insensitive substring match.
#
# The point of keeping it OUT of git: a checker that hard-codes your private folder
# names would publish exactly what it is meant to hide.
#
# Good candidates:
#   - your sample-library folder names
#   - machine / host names on your network
#   - your username, if it differs from anything already public in NOTICE
#   - client or project names under NDA
#
# Silence a false positive with "# noqa: private" on that line.

# my-sample-pack-folder
# my-desktop-name
